  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 6a38c3767fef3e942bd84ac654ade706, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::TutorialLines
  texts:
  - self: 0
    lines:
    - When you click on a duck you will get to see their age, hunger level, and how
      happy they are.
    - You can also click and hold to grab a duck and drag them around.
    - "It\u2019s pretty bare around here though, click the hammer when you are ready
      to build something."
  - self: 1
    lines:
    - This is the general happiness of Quacklands.
    - Above is the general hunger and below is the time until the next duck month.
  - self: 2
    lines:
    - Crumbies are earned in passing by ducks and the amount of crumbies you have
      is in the top left corner.
  - self: 3
    lines:
    - Here are plans for buildings that can be created to spruce up the place.
    - "Each build has a requirement that will benefit our \u201Clovely\u201D community."
    - "Each build costs a certain amount of crumbies so don\u2019t get too trigger
      happy."
  - self: 4
    lines:
    - This is your file cabinet which gives you access to your notepad, newspaper,
      and upgrade log.
    - The notepad will give you the juicy gossip of the day to day life of your ducks!
      My specialty.
    - The newspaper shows what you have done for the community and gets updated after
      every duck month.
    - The upgrade log shows you what upgrades your civilization has gotten.
  - self: 5
    lines:
    - If you ever need a breather just press the pause button to stop time.
    - If you ever get one of those days where you feel like time is just dragging
      on just use this fast forward to kick things up a notch.
  - self: 6
    lines:
    - Here is the dining hall where the ducks come to eat the crumbies we have collected.
    - When the dining hall is empty ducks need to deposit crumbies into it.
